formula:
  title: "RFC 4122 Version 4 UUID Structure"
  expression: "xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx (where y ∈ {8, 9, a, b})"
  explanation: "A Version 4 UUID consists of 128 bits: 4 bits are fixed for the version (0100 for v4), 2 bits specify the variant (10 for RFC 4122), and the remaining 122 bits are filled with cryptographically strong pseudorandom numbers. With 2¹²² possible combinations (approximately 5.3 × 10³⁶), the probability of collision is negligible."
workedExamples:
